      "title": "To W. B. Tegetmeier 21 [February 1859]",
      "header_text": [
        "To W. B. Tegetmeier 21 [February 1859]Down Bromley Kent21"
      ],
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "body_paragraph": 1,
          "text": "Here is a misfortune: the silver Spangled Hamburgh Hen was seen quite well this morning & half an hour afterwards was found stone-dead on her back. If you could get me 2 or 3 more Hens, it would be very useful for my little experiment.— Perhaps you will have forgotten what I have: they are as follows. The Spanish Cock 2 White Games 1 White Cochin 1 Silk Fowl 1 Silver Poland",
          "html_class": "",
          "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 1"
        },
        {
          "body_paragraph": 2,
          "text": "Before very long I must begin & save eggs.",
          "html_class": "",
          "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 2"
        },
        {
          "body_paragraph": 3,
          "text": "I hope your Bee Soc. flourishes. I gave your paper to Mr Knight Bruce, (son of the Vice-Chancellor) & he seemed very enthusiastic & inclined to join it.—",
          "html_class": "",
          "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 3"
        },
        {
          "body_paragraph": 4,
          "text": "I have been extra poorly of late & returned only on Saturday from a fortnight of Hydropathy.—",
          "html_class": "",
          "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 4"
        },
        {
          "body_paragraph": 5,
          "text": "Believe me, my dear Sir | Yours very sincerely | C. Darwin",
          "html_class": "",
          "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 5"
        }
      ],
      "excluded_body_annotations_and_salutations": [
        {
          "class": "salute",
          "text": "My dear Sir"
        }
      ],
      "body_container_count": 1,
      "used_whole_body_fallback": false,
      "editorial_summary": "Summary Sends list of poultry breeds he would like.",
      "editorial_footnotes": "Footnotes1See letters to W. B. Tegetmeier, 16 November [1858], 27 [November 1858], and 24 December [1858].2Tegetmeier was the secretary of the Apiarian Society of London (Richardson 1916, p. 47). Tegetmeier may have asked CD to be a patron of the society (see letter to W. B. Tegetmeier,2 October [1858]).3Louis Knight Bruce, who lived in Keston, near Down, was the son of James Lewis Knight Bruce, the lord justice and vice-chancellor from 1841. Knight Bruce was a bee-keeper and had assisted CD in his study of bees’ cells (see letters to W. B. Tegetmeier, 14 April [1858] and [21 April 1858]).4CD returned to Down from Moor Park hydropathic establishment on 19 February 1859 (‘Journal’; Appendix II).",
      "letter_container_present": true
    },
