      "title": "To W. B. Tegetmeier 5 March [1859]1",
      "header_text": [
        "To W. B. Tegetmeier 5 March [1859]1Down Bromley KentMarch 5th"
      ],
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "body_paragraph": 1,
          "text": "The fowls arrived quite hearty yesterday & are very pretty.— I am now sufficiently stocked, thanks to your great kindness. diag Former Fowls.— 13",
          "html_class": "",
          "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 1"
        },
        {
          "body_paragraph": 2,
          "text": "Hamburgh 10.6",
          "html_class": "",
          "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 2"
        },
        {
          "body_paragraph": 3,
          "text": "Basket 1",
          "html_class": "",
          "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 3"
        },
        {
          "body_paragraph": 4,
          "text": "£ 1.4.6ramme which I now enclose.—",
          "html_class": "",
          "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 4"
        },
        {
          "body_paragraph": 5,
          "text": "You shall hear result of experiment.—",
          "html_class": "",
          "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 5"
        },
        {
          "body_paragraph": 6,
          "text": "Mr K. Bruce told me he would join the Bee Socy.— & I will remind him whenever I see him.",
          "html_class": "",
          "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 6"
        },
        {
          "body_paragraph": 7,
          "text": "With my renewed thanks, pray believe me | Yours very sincerely | C. Darwin",
          "html_class": "",
          "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 7"
        },
        {
          "body_paragraph": 8,
          "text": "When you see Mr Weir do not forget to ask about wing-bars &c in silver Barbs.—",
          "html_class": "",
          "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 8"
        }
      ],
      "excluded_body_annotations_and_salutations": [
        {
          "class": "salute",
          "text": "My dear Sir"
        }
      ],
      "body_container_count": 1,
      "used_whole_body_fallback": false,
      "editorial_summary": "Summary Sends payment for poultry received.",
      "editorial_footnotes": "Footnotes1Dated by an entry in CD’s Account book (Down House MS) recording a payment to Tegetmeier for the amount mentioned in the letter (see n. 2, below).2CD recorded a payment of £1 4s. 6d. for ‘Tegetmeier Poultry’ on 2 March 1859 in his Account book (Down House MS).3The experiment was to ascertain whether the colour of the ancestral Gallus bankiva could be obtained by crossing existing breeds of domestic poultry. The results were described in Variation 1: 240–3.4See letter to W. B. Tegetmeier, 21 [February 1859].5CD had been anxious to question Harrison William Weir about the colouring of pigeons for some time. See letters to W. B. Tegetmeier, 2 October [1858] and 27 [November 1858]. Black wing-bars are characteristic of the wild, ancestral pigeon, Columba livia, which is slate-blue in colour. CD had been informed that wing-bars appear almost without exception in all blue domestic breeds, but he had not yet recorded a case among barbs.",
      "letter_container_present": true
    },
